$ heat --help
usage: heat [--nx N] [--steps N] [--cfl CFL] [--scheme value] [--threads value] [--verbose]... [--save [value]] [--help] [--markdown] [--version]

Solve the 2D heat equation on a square plate

Optional switches:
  --nx N
      default value 64
      Cells along each direction
  --steps N
      default value 100
      Time steps
  --cfl CFL
      range (0, 0.5]
      default value 0.25
      CFL number
  --scheme value, -s value
      choices: fe, cn
      default value fe
      Time scheme: explicit Euler or Crank-Nicolson
  --threads value
      range [1, 64]
      default value 1
      OpenMP threads
  --verbose, -v
      default value 0
      Verbosity (repeatable)
  --save [value]
      choices: vtk, csv
      default value vtk
      Save the solution (format: vtk, csv)
  --help, -h
      Print this help message
  --markdown, -md
      Save this help message in a Markdown file
  --version
      Print version
